  "overall_correctness": "correct",
  "overall_explanation": "Implementation review confirms the patch is correct, thoroughly contained, and satisfies all requirements R01–R09 without introducing breaking integration bugs across CLI or adapter boundaries:\n\n- R01 (in-spec): Resolves the installer exception, SOUL pollution, and unsolicited six-MCP server registration in Hermes; Windows default home correctly points to LOCALAPPDATA/hermes while explicit HERMES_HOME is honored; non-OMP adapters explicitly state that routine tasks do not require coding ceremony.\n- R02 (in-spec): Retains a single npm package managing host-specific profiles across all eight named adapters and declarative custom hosts; automated native review remains strictly bounded to OMP with Bun.\n- R03 (in-spec): Inspection is read-only, spawning zero host processes or paid inference; capability evidence is partitioned into documented, configured, declared, and unknown; evidenced native mechanisms are reused without imposing parallel task boards, second delegation loops, or unconditional dashboards.\n- R04 (in-spec): Explicit capability gaps enable portable workflow commands (T0/T1 start, recon artifact, check, close) and worktree integration when Git is present; unknown is treated as unknown rather than absence, avoiding speculative dependency installs.\n- R05 (in-spec): The declarative schema1 custom host contract requires project-relative instructionsFile and strictly declarative capabilities; executable commands, path traversal, control characters, and ADS streams fail closed during validation.\n- R06 (in-spec): Deterministic consumer tests verify installation and rollback across platforms; overhead reductions (prompt bytes, MCP count, skill entries) are accounted for separately while general AI quality improvements remain honestly labeled not-proven without live paid A/B.\n- R07 (in-spec): Default non-OMP policy is direct and usable for general tasks without mandatory state machines; OMP native strict workflow and review boundaries remain preserved.\n- R08 (in-spec): Containment guards prevent writes outside target roots and user homes; ambient host roots outside isolated userHome are ignored; Hermes profile selection requires live identity files.\n- R09 (in-spec): No paid model inference or live benchmarks were dispatched; native runtime unavailability is explicitly acknowledged as not-verified.\n\nLean/simplification lens observation:\n- `delete:` unused `unlinkSync` import in `tools/task-claim.mjs` (line 10), replacement: nothing. net: -1 lines possible.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.98
}

